# Society Canyon — local dev environment
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. R2 is the intended storage driver for BOTH
# local dev and production (dev/prod parity). See README section 7.

# --- OpenAI (required) ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Realtime voice model. Defaults to gpt-realtime-mini (cheaper/faster).
# Set to gpt-realtime for the full model.
# OPENAI_REALTIME_MODEL=gpt-realtime-mini
#
# Text-mode chat model (dev-iteration console). Defaults to gpt-4o-mini.
# OPENAI_TEXT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# --- Image generation cost controls (this is where the money goes) ---
# Defaults to gpt-image-1-mini at "medium" quality — roughly 8-12x cheaper
# per image than gpt-image-1 with quality left unset. "low" quality was
# tested and rejected: it loses the pixel-art texture and renders as a smooth
# painterly illustration instead. "medium" is the cheapest tier that still
# reads as genuine pixel art. Drop to "low" for max savings if style fidelity
# matters less than cost, or raise to "high" for a specific polished session.
# OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1-mini
# OPENAI_IMAGE_QUALITY=medium   # low | medium | high

# --- Local image generation (ComfyUI, free/offline alternative to OpenAI images) ---
# When set to "comfyui", image-generate and image-scene render through a local
# ComfyUI server instead of OpenAI's images API. Requires a running ComfyUI
# instance (see ComfyUI-master/) with sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors in
# models/checkpoints/ and the nerijs pixel-art-xl LoRA in models/loras/ to
# match the existing 64-bit pixel art aesthetic. Scene proposals (the text
# step) still use OPENAI_API_KEY regardless of this setting.
# Start the server first: cd ComfyUI-master && ./venv/bin/python main.py --port 8188
# On Apple-Silicon MPS a 1536x1024 SDXL image takes ~90-180s; tune COMFY_STEPS
# down for speed. COMFY_TIMEOUT_MS must exceed a full generation.
# IMAGE_PROVIDER=comfyui
# COMFY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8188
# COMFY_CHECKPOINT=sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors
# COMFY_LORA=pixel-art-xl.safetensors
# COMFY_VAE=sdxl_vae_fp16_fix.safetensors
# COMFY_STEPS=20
# COMFY_TIMEOUT_MS=360000

# --- Open Voice pipeline (uncensored, self-hosted alternative to Voice mode) ---
# Whisper (STT, via OPENAI_API_KEY above) -> OpenRouter open-weight LLM -> local
# Pocket-TTS (free, Kyutai, runs on this machine). Used by the "Open Voice"
# console mode. See README for setup (uv tool install pocket-tts; pocket-tts
# serve --port 8123 must be running for this mode to work).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=thedrummer/cydonia-24b-v4.1
#
# Pocket-TTS server URL (must be running locally, or point at a remote host
# once deployed). Defaults to http://localhost:8123.
# POCKET_TTS_URL=http://localhost:8123
#
# Default voice: "Watercooler" from Unmute.sh's demo — VCTK speaker p329.
# Requires accepting terms at https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts and
# running `uvx hf auth login` once (voice-cloning is gated; without auth,
# Pocket-TTS falls back to its smaller built-in-only voice catalog).
# POCKET_TTS_VOICE=hf://kyutai/tts-voices/vctk/p329_023.wav

# --- Cloudflare R2 storage (required for durable sessions + images) ---
# All four R2_* vars must be set together, or the app falls back to LOCAL
# filesystem storage (data/), which is NOT durable on serverless hosts.
R2_ENDPOINT=https://<accountid>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=society-canyon

# --- Optional ---
# Force local filesystem storage for offline dev (silences the R2 warning).
# STORAGE_DRIVER=local
#
# NOTE: A public bucket / R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL is no longer required — generated
# images are streamed through the app at /api/media/<key>, which works with a
# private bucket in every environment.
